  { icon: 'ph:certificate', title: 'State licensing', body: 'Signed attendance records, fire drill and shelter-in-place logs, allergy and medication rosters.' },
  { icon: 'ph:calculator', title: 'Tax', body: 'The IRS home-daycare time-space percentage, which needs both business hours and the square footage used for them.' },
];

// Why 8pm-from-memory is a product problem and not a habit problem.
const problems = [
  { icon: 'ph:brain', title: 'Memory isn’t reliable', body: 'A nap logged from memory at 8pm is a guess, and so is a diaper change. The records that matter most legally are the least accurate ones.' },
  { icon: 'ph:door-open', title: 'It wears providers down', body: 'Many providers leave this work because of the paperwork. The goal was to give them their evenings back.' },
  { icon: 'ph:clock-countdown', title: 'Problems surface too late', body: 'Finding out at month end that a lunch was missing a vegetable is too late to do anything about it.' },
