  <Section tone="paper" padding="default" id="heuristics" class="scroll-mt-24">
    <Container width="content">
      <div class="case-layout">
        <div class="case-layout__head">
          <Heading level={2} visual="display-md" tone="ink">Scoring the app against Nielsen’s heuristics</Heading>
        </div>
        <div class="case-layout__body">
          <div class="mt-8 measure space-y-5 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted text-lg">
            <p>
              A consistent look isn’t the same as a usable app, so I scored Logatot
              against Nielsen’s ten usability heuristics, from 0 to 10. I captured
              every public and signed-in page, 119 in all, at desktop width and the
              core pages at phone width, and tied every finding to a file and line.
            </p>
            <p>
              The lowest scores weren’t about looks. Error prevention and error
              recovery both scored 3, mostly because of one hidden cause: the app
              loads htmx instead of Turbo, so every Rails confirm prompt and
              double-submit guard silently did nothing. Fixing that once, in a shared
              layer, fixed it on every page.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-2 gap-8 py-8">
            <Metric value="4.9" label="average score before" caption="across ten heuristics and 119 page captures" />
            <Metric value="3" label="lowest scores" caption="error prevention and recovering from errors" />
          </div>

          <div class="mt-12">
            <p class="mono-label mb-2">By heuristic</p>
            <p class="mb-6 text-sm text-ink-muted">Score before the fixes, and what changed.</p>
            <ol class="border-t border-line">
              {heuristics.map((h) => (
                <li class="border-b border-line py-4">
                  <div class="flex items-baseline gap-4">
                    <span class="w-8 shrink-0 font-mono text-xs text-ink-muted">H{h.n}</span>
                    <span class="min-w-0 flex-1 font-medium text-ink">{h.name}</span>
                    <span class="font-mono text-sm text-ink whitespace-nowrap" aria-label={`scored ${h.before} out of 10 before`}>
                      {h.before}<span class="text-ink-muted">/10</span>
                    </span>
                  </div>
                  <p class="mt-1 pl-12 text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">{h.fix}</p>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ol>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Container>

    <Container width="content" class="mt-16">
      <div class="case-layout-cont measure space-y-5 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted text-lg">
        <p>
          One finding wasn’t about usability at all. Leftover scaffold pages from
          early development could show data across accounts. Those routes were removed
          first, before any usability work, and a test now visits every page to make
          sure none of them returns a server error.
        </p>
        <p>
          The fixes are in, but I haven’t re-scored the app yet, so this page only
          shows the starting scores. The re-score is the next step.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

